# Lending Loan
# Example Business Knowledge expressed in Menata Language
# Domain: Lending — an approved, disbursed loan whose repayment schedule is generated
# as a whole series at once, not one record at a time
# Case 14 of the Case Portfolio (runtime/case-portfolio.md)
# References: lending-loan-application.menata, lending-repayment-schedule-entry.menata
#
# THE NEW FINDING THIS CASE EXISTS TO SURFACE: Disburse below must create an entire
# series of future-dated Repayment Schedule Entries (one per month of Term Months,
# each with its own Due Date and principal/interest split) computed from a single
# formula. Every prior action either creates ONE record (CAP-A06) or computes ONE
# value (CAP-A02/A11/A14) — nothing names generating N related records from a formula
# in a single action.

Loan

Fields

- Application : Loan Application
- Principal : Money
- Interest Rate : Number
- Term Months : Number
- Disbursed At : Date
- Status : Active | Closed | Defaulted

Events

When Disburse

    Disbursed At Today

    Generate Repayment Schedule

    Status Active

Constraints

- Application is required.
- Principal is required.
- Term Months is required.

Permissions

Loan Officer

- Disburse

Views

- Loan Form : Form
- Active Loans : List
- Loan Detail : Detail
